<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Lostman Trail and Loop (from Trillium Lake Sno-Park)</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:147-4: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="45.285259" lon="-121.727970"><ele>1156.8</ele><name>Trillium Lake Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:trillium-lake-sno-park (OSM parking way/148019331); confidence: high; pdf_page: 143; book_elev_ft: 3830</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.280208" lon="-121.733236"><ele>1103.1</ele><name>Airstrip junction</name><desc>source: as in or-vielbig-2e_142-2: OSM junction of NF 2656 and NF 2650-131; confidence: high; pdf_page: 144</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.270371" lon="-121.732742"><ele>1103.9</ele><name>Campground junction</name><desc>source: OSM node 37397443, north end of the Trillium Lake Loop Road (NF 2656, USFS SNO-2656B Mud Creek Loop Nordic) on Trillium Lake Road east of the lake; confidence: high; pdf_page: 146; quote: From the campground junction east of Trillium Lake (see map) take the road angling uphill</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.247584" lon="-121.738954"><ele>1191.7</ele><name>Jefferson Viewpoint</name><desc>source: OSM node 37598733, the sweeping turn of NF 2656 from south to east, 1.8 mi along the road from the campground junction (DEM 3,910 ft vs the book 3,940); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 146; book_elev_ft: 3940; quote: a long, gentle climb to the Jefferson Viewpoint, 1.8 miles from the junction and 3.5 miles from the sno-park ... The road makes a sweeping turn at the viewpoint</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.243053" lon="-121.733122"><ele>1211.2</ele><name>High Divide (Lostman Trail start)</name><desc>source: OSM node 2452534627, north end of the Lost Man Trail (piste way 237335916; USFS SNO-762 Lost Man Nordic, road 2656254) on NF 2656, 0.5 mi past the viewpoint; confidence: high; pdf_page: 150; quote: Follow the Mud Creek Ridge road 0.6 mile beyond the Jefferson Viewpoint to the High Divide ... the Lostman Trail is the obvious side road to the left (east)</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.232076" lon="-121.741755"><ele>1149.2</ele><name>Lostman Trail meets the High Divide road</name><desc>source: OSM node 2452545080, south end of the Lost Man Trail on NF 2656, 0.3 mi above Big Bend; confidence: high; pdf_page: 150; quote: Ultimately you will reach the High Divide road where you turn north and return to the Jefferson Viewpoint.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.243053" lon="-121.733122"><ele>1211.2</ele><name>High Divide (return)</name><desc>source: as above; confidence: high; pdf_page: 150</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.247584" lon="-121.738954"><ele>1191.7</ele><name>Jefferson Viewpoint (return)</name><desc>source: as above; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 150</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.270371" lon="-121.732742"><ele>1103.9</ele><name>Campground junction (return)</name><desc>source: as above; confidence: high</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.280208" lon="-121.733236"><ele>1103.1</ele><name>Airstrip junction (return)</name><desc>source: as above; confidence: high</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.285259" lon="-121.727970"><ele>1156.8</ele><name>Trillium Lake Sno-Park (finish)</name><desc>source: as start; confidence: high</desc></wpt>
